From fe93b380c56412ba699ea31870a0beed372160c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:17:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 77/83] thermal: gov_step_wise: drop the request of a trip that
 needs no mitigation

When the zone temperature is below a trip's threshold and falling,
get_target_state() asks for the instance's lower state and returns
THERMAL_NO_TARGET only at a later update, once the current state of the
cooling device is at or below that lower state.

That is not reliable in two cases:

- The cooling device is shared with other thermal zones. Its current
  state can be held above instance->lower by another zone, so an
  instance whose trip was never crossed starts to request its lower
  state as soon as its zone sees a falling temperature.
- The zone is not polled. Once its last passive trip has been left there
  is no further update and the request for instance->lower stays until
  the next sensor interrupt.

On the OnePlus Pad 4 both come together: the CPU zones (tsens, interrupt
driven) have a map with a lower state of 14 on their 112 C trip, and the
skin zone holds the same cpufreq cooling devices at state 18-22 under
load. After the load both clusters stay at state 14 (1.9 / 2.67 GHz
instead of 3.6 / 4.4 GHz) with every zone far below its trips.
Reproduced with thermal emulation alone: skin zone above its upper trip,
one CPU zone per cluster 90 -> 80 C, skin emulation off: state 14 / 14
stays.

No mitigation is necessary in that branch, so return THERMAL_NO_TARGET
at once. A polled zone reaches the same cooling state one polling period
earlier; with a lower state of 0 nothing changes for the cooling device.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/thermal/gov_step_wise.c | 19 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/gov_step_wise.c b/drivers/thermal/gov_step_wise.c
index ea277c466..9921d8c82 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/gov_step_wise.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/gov_step_wise.c
@@ -25,9 +25,8 @@
  *       minimum
  * If the temperature is lower than a trip point,
  *    a. if the trend is THERMAL_TREND_RAISING, do nothing
- *    b. if the trend is THERMAL_TREND_DROPPING, use the minimum applicable
- *       cooling state for this trip point, or if the cooling state already
- *       equals lower limit, deactivate the thermal instance
+ *    b. if the trend is THERMAL_TREND_DROPPING, deactivate the thermal
+ *       instance
  */
 static unsigned long get_target_state(struct thermal_instance *instance,
 				enum thermal_trend trend, bool throttle)
@@ -65,14 +64,16 @@ static unsigned long get_target_state(struct thermal_instance *instance,
 				     min(instance->lower + 1, instance->upper),
 				     instance->upper);
 	} else if (trend == THERMAL_TREND_DROPPING) {
-		if (cur_state <= instance->lower)
-			return THERMAL_NO_TARGET;
-
 		/*
-		 * If 'throttle' is false, no mitigation is necessary, so
-		 * request the lower state for this instance.
+		 * If 'throttle' is false, no mitigation is necessary, so drop
+		 * the request of this instance. Asking for instance->lower first
+		 * and dropping the request at a later update is not reliable:
+		 * the current state of a cooling device shared with other zones
+		 * can be held above instance->lower by them, and a zone without
+		 * polling is not updated again after its last passive trip has
+		 * been left, so the request for instance->lower would stay.
 		 */
-		return instance->lower;
+		return THERMAL_NO_TARGET;
 	}
 
 	return instance->target;
